  "theorem_name": "FiniteCongruenceFixedRootWindowNoGo",
  "declared_proposition": "Let B_1(u,v) be the TICKET-258 degree-17 coefficient form. For every integer modulus M>=2 and every nonempty rational interval I contained in (-1,0), there are infinitely many primitive pairs (u,v) with v>0, u/v in I, u^2-2v^2<0, and B_1(u,v)=1 modulo M. Consequently no finite collection of coefficient congruences, even supplemented by primitivity, the admissible norm sign, and any fixed root window, can exclude the remaining unit-coefficient branch.",
  "mathematical_argument": "Replace finitely many moduli by their least common multiple M. For arbitrarily large N set v=M^N. The interval vI eventually has length greater than M, so it contains u congruent to one modulo M. Every prime divisor of v divides M, while u is one modulo M, hence gcd(u,v)=1. Since I is contained in (-1,0), the norm u^2-2v^2 is negative. All terms of B_1(u,v) except u^17 contain v, so B_1(u,v) is congruent to u^17, hence to one modulo M. The witnesses are only local: exact equality forces the scale-dependent q^(-17) approximation from TICKET-258, which a fixed interval does not encode.",
  "result_classification": "exact_no_go",
  "problem_status": "open_not_proven",
